w-dropping ride","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"non-commissionable transit anchoring paid Arví add-ons","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Botero Plaza + Museo de Antioquia","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC-guided downtown add-on / activity affiliate","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/comuna-13-medellin-2026-street-art-transformation-tour.htm (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Downtown plaza of monumental Fernando Botero bronzes beside the region''s flagship art museum — pair with a morning Comuna 13 tour via the metro","si":"culture","blurb":"Downtown plaza of monumental Fernando Botero bronzes beside the region''s flagship art museum — pair with a morning Comuna 13 tour via the metro","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC-guided downtown add-on / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Guatapé + El Peñol rock (740 steps) + zócalos","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"day-trip operator affiliate / DMC","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Medellin/Guatape-and-Penol-Rock-Full-Day-Tour/d4563-6033P27 (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"~2 hrs east: climb the monolith over the island-studded reservoir, then wander Guatapé''s brightly painted zócalo streets and lakeside lunch","si":"expedition","blurb":"~2 hrs east: climb the monolith over the island-studded reservoir, then wander Guatapé''s brightly painted zócalo streets and lakeside lunch","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"day-trip operator affiliate / DMC","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Jardín & Jericó coffee pueblos + working-finca coffee tour","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC / coffee-hacienda MoR stay","source":"https://two.travel/experiences/medellin-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Postcard Antioquian towns south of the city — plaza culture, cloud forest, and coffee at source with a finca tour/tasting","si":"expedition","blurb":"Postcard Antioquian towns south of the city — plaza culture, cloud forest, and coffee at source with a finca tour/tasting","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"DMC / coffee-hacienda MoR stay","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Paragliding the Aburrá Valley (San Félix)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"activity affiliate / DMC (operator-vetted only)","source":"https://two.travel/experiences/medellin-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Tandem flight over the whole Medellín bowl — operator-vetted","si":"expedition","blurb":"Tandem flight over the whole Medellín bowl — operator-vetted","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"activity affiliate / DMC (operator-vetted only)","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"El Poblado / Provenza & Manila dining","si_tag":"CUL","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC dining add-ons / hotel F&B / activity affiliate","source":"https://two.travel/experiences/medellin-travel-guide/ (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Al-fresco brunches, world-class cocktail bars, Colombian tasting menus, Japanese-Colombian fusion, specialty coffee","si":"culinary","blurb":"Al-fresco brunches, world-class cocktail bars, Colombian tasting menus, Japanese-Colombian fusion, specialty coffee","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"DMC dining add-ons / hotel F&B / activity affiliate","accessed":"2026-07-07"},{"name":"Feria de las Flores — silleteros (Jul 31–Aug 9, 2026)","si_tag":"RHN/CHER","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC festival packages + hotel/villa MoR","source":"https://medellingroup.com/blog/feria-de-las-flores-2026-complete-guide-to-medellins-flower-festival (Accessed 2026-07-07)","timing":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"The flower festival and its 530-silletero parade — the city''s headline peak; grandstand + curated hotel packages","si":"RHN/CHER","blurb":"The flower festival and its 530-silletero parade — the city''s headline peak; grandstand + curated hotel packages","when":"[''December–March '', ''July–August '', ''Feria de las Flores late-Jul→Aug 9 '', ''December Alumbrados '']","commission":"DMC festival packages + hotel/villa MoR","accessed":"2026-07-07"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Medellín a good place for a couples trip or honeymoon?","a":"Yes — for couples arriving together. El Poblado luxury apartments, rooftop-pool hotels and coffee-finca escapes are genuinely romantic. The plain caveat: the US Embassy links 8 suspicious US-citizen deaths in Medellín (Nov–Dec 2023) to dating-app-lured druggings, so the safe lane is partners who arrive together, not app meet-ups.","source":"co.usembassy.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What is Comuna 13 and is it worth visiting?","a":"Yes — Comuna 13 is Medellín''s most-visited site and the emblem of its turnaround. Outdoor public escalators installed in 2011 cut a 35-minute climb to 6 minutes; today the hillside barrio is a canvas of community murals, told on a guided walking tour (~$20–30). Go guided, daytime, as a group.","source":"machupicchu.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How do you visit Guatapé and El Peñol rock from Medellín?","a":"Guatapé sits about 2 hours east, usually as a full-day trip. The headline is climbing El Peñol (Piedra del Peñol) via 740 steps — most reach the top in 15–25 minutes — over a reservoir dotted with islands, then wandering the brightly painted zócalo streets. Book a day-trip operator or DMC.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"adventure"},{"q":"Is Medellín safe to visit right now?","a":"Colombia is at US State Dept Level 3 \"Reconsider Travel\" (issued 2026-03-31, codes C·T·U·K·N), but Medellín/Antioquia are NOT in any named Level-4 Do-Not-Travel area — those are Arauca, Cauca (excl. Popayán), Valle del Cauca (excl. Cali), Norte de Santander, and within ~10 km of the Venezuela border. Medellín has direct air via MDE/Rionegro.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Medellín?","a":"The signature Medellín danger is dating-app drugging-and-robbery, not the headlines. The US Embassy is aware of 8 suspicious US-citizen deaths (Nov 1–Dec 31, 2023) involving scopolamine (\"burundanga\") — odorless, memory-erasing and lethal in large doses. Don''t meet app strangers alone, never leave a drink unattended, and meet only in public.","source":"co.usembassy.gov, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is climbing El Peñol''s 740 steps dangerous?","a":"It''s a steep but manageable self-guided climb — 740 steps, 15–25 minutes for most — though not for those with cardiac or mobility limits. Pace it, hydrate, and mind your footing on the descent. Paragliding over the Aburrá Valley, by contrast, should be flown only with certified, insured, safety-vetted operators.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Medellín & Antioquia Travel Guide 2026 — Comuna 13, Guatapé, Coffee Country | TravelWell","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-CO","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Medellín","Comuna 13 tour","Guatapé Peñol","Feria de las Flores","dónde hospedarse en Medellín","seguridad Medellín aplicaciones de citas"],"hreflang":["en","es-CO"],"author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07","primary_keyword":"Medellín & Antioquia"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"The Charlee","location":"El Poblado","note":"Envy rooftop pool/bar, 360° valley views; most-photographed hotel in Colombia","program":"MoR / consortia where preferred","price_tier":"$$$$"},{"name":"Diez Hotel Categoría Colombia","location":"El Poblado","note":"Colombian-art boutique, full-service spa","program":"MoR / consortia where preferred","price_tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"The Click Clack Hotel Medellín","location":"El Poblado","note":"Design-forward, artisan interiors, rooftop; Mr & Mrs Smith listed","program":"MoR / consortia where preferred","price_tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"Luxury coffee-country haciendas (Hacienda Bambusa / Sazagua-tier)","location":"Antioquia / Coffee-Triangle-adjacent","note":"Rural ultra pairing","program":"MoR","price_tier":"$$$-$$$$"},{"name":"NOTE — Four Seasons Casa Medina","location":"Bogotá (NOT Medellín)","note":"Do not misassign to Medellín","program":"n/a","price_tier":"$$$$"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Medellín & Antioquia, Colombia, Colombia"},"geo":{"lat":6.2442,"lng":-75.5812}}'::jsonb, 66),
  ('mendoza-argentina', '10S', 'Mendoza & the Wine Country, Argentina', 'Argentina', 'Malbec born a thousand metres up, poured under the', 'live', 'verified', 'restaurant', 'Northwest, Mendoza Wine & Iguazú', '{"culinary","romance","expedition"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":null,"safety":{"emergency":"911","advisory_level":"L1","advisory_updated":"2026-05-20","regional_exception":"Level 2 — city of Rosario only (~1,000 km from Mendoza)","book_enabled":true,"consent_flow":false,"bin":"freely bookable (L1)","air_access_verified":true,"air_access_note":"Mendoza El Plumerillo (MDZ) via Buenos Aires (AEP/EZE)","trauma":"excellent Mendoza private clinics (English-speaking); severe trauma escalates to Buenos Aires + international evac; carry medical/evac insurance","drink_drive":"always a designated driver or guided wine tour with transport — never self-drive between tastings","altitude":"Alta Montaña day trip ~2,700 m (mild); Aconcagua summit mountaineering is expedition-grade, guided + permitted","rafting":"Mendoza River (Potrerillos) Class II–IV; certified guides mandatory","water":"potable in Mendoza city/major towns; bottled/treated in remote areas"},"timing":{"peak":"late Feb–April (harvest / Fiesta Nacional de la Vendimia; 2026 central acts Mar 6–10) + autumn Mar–Apr","secondary_peak":"Oct–Nov (spring; ~15–25% below harvest rates)","inflection":"book icon wineries/lodges 3–4 months ahead of Feb–April peak; demand inflects at Vendimia-calendar release (Jan) and ~90 days out","fire_date":"curve-start minus 1–2 weeks — late Jan → mid-Feb for March/Vendimia trips; late Sept for Oct–Nov spring window","off_season_fill":"winter Jun–Aug — Andes ski (Los Penitentes/Penitentes, Jun–Sep) + Cacheuta thermal wellness + indoor-cellar tastings"},"jewels":[{"name":"Valle de Uco icon estates + long lunch (Zuccardi Piedra Infinita, Salentein + Kilka)","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC winery day 10–20% / affiliate 4–8%","source":"https://www.mrwinery.com/tour/visit-zuccardi-piedra-infinita-and-have-lunch-at-bodega","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20% / affiliate 4–8%"},{"name":"The Vines estate tasting + vine-side table","si_tag":"culinary+romance","tier":"ultra","commission_path":"DMC / lodge package 10–20%","source":"https://www.scottdunn.com/us/argentina/hotels/the-vines-resort-spa","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the resort''s own vineyard program and vine-side dining, a natural CUL+RHM crossover","si":"culinary+romance","blurb":"the resort''s own vineyard program and vine-side dining, a natural CUL+RHM crossover","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"DMC / lodge package 10–20%"},{"name":"Luján de Cuyo classic Malbec cellars","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC winery day 10–20%","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/lujan-de-cuyo-from-mendoza-wine-route-2026-malbec-guide.htm","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"the historic, powerful, ripe Luján style; best infrastructure + easiest access from the city","si":"culinary","blurb":"the historic, powerful, ripe Luján style; best infrastructure + easiest access from the city","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20%"},{"name":"Catena Zapata pyramid + Blending Games","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","commission_path":"private-transport DMC/affiliate 4–20%","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Mendoza/Catena-Zapata-Wine-Tour-from-Mendoza/d931-5693P18","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the Maya-pyramid-inspired icon bodega; the signature experience lets guests build their own blend guided by experts","si":"culinary","blurb":"the Maya-pyramid-inspired icon bodega; the signature experience lets guests build their own blend guided by experts","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"private-transport DMC/affiliate 4–20%"},{"name":"Maipú bike-and-wine + olive-oil & asado","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"essential","commission_path":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/mendoza-travel-guide-2026-argentinas-wine-capital.htm","hook":"the casual, cyclable Maipú route linking Malbec, Bonarda, olive oil, gourmet estates, and a wood-fired asado","si":"culinary","blurb":"the casual, cyclable Maipú route linking Malbec, Bonarda, olive oil, gourmet estates, and a wood-fired asado","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%"},{"name":"Achaval-Ferrer single-vineyard Malbec","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC winery day 10–20%","source":"https://www.machupicchu.org/mendoza-wine-tours-2026-best-wineries-tastings.htm","si":"culinary","commission":"DMC winery day 10–20%"},{"name":"Sunrise hot-air balloon over the vineyards","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"affiliate 4–8% / DMC bundle","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/argentina-l168992/hot-air-balloon-ride-over-mendoza-s-vineyards-wine-toast-t876044/","hook":"~45–60 min float from the Junín/Barriales area over vine rows and olive groves with the Andes on the horizon, sparkling-wine toast on landing","si":"romance","blurb":"~45–60 min float from the Junín/Barriales area over vine rows and olive groves with the Andes on the horizon, sparkling-wine toast on landing","commission":"affiliate 4–8% / DMC bundle"},{"name":"Cacheuta thermal springs","si_tag":"romance+wellness","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"affiliate spa day 4–8% / DMC","source":"https://thewholeworldornothing.com/hot-springs-mendoza-cacheuta-thermal-baths/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","si":"romance+wellness","blurb":"natural Andean hot springs on the Mendoza River, multi-temperature stone pools, Argentina''s only grotto sauna, mud baths, and a Creole asado buffet","when":"year-round","commission":"affiliate spa day 4–8% / DMC"},{"name":"Alta Montaña + Aconcagua viewpoint + Puente del Inca","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC / affiliate day 4–20%","source":"https://www.getyourguide.com/mendoza-l673/andes-day-trip-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-t55889/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","si":"expedition","blurb":"Route 7 full-day: Potrerillos Dam, Uspallata, Puente del Inca''s natural stone-and-hot-spring formation, and the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC / affiliate day 4–20%"},{"name":"Mendoza River rafting (Potrerillos)","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"essential","commission_path":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%","source":"https://solsalute.com/blog/adventure-tourism-in-potrerillos-mendoza/","timing":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","si":"expedition","blurb":"Class II–IV depending on season/flow; certified rescue guides, kayak support, and full safety kit standard. Guided: mandatory — never run this river unguided","when":"late Feb–April  + autumn Mar–Apr","commission":"affiliate / DMC 4–15%"},{"name":"Uspallata & the high desert","si_tag":"expedition","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC day 10–20%","source":"https://www.myguideargentina.com/experiences/mendoza-uspallata-aconcagua-and-puente-del-inca-day-trip","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","si":"expedition","blurb":"cinematic Andean valley, gateway between the wine plain and the summit corridor; horseback and 4x4 add-ons","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC day 10–20%"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Mendoza the world''s Malbec capital?","a":"Because the concentration is unmatched: Argentina holds roughly 75% of the world''s Malbec vines, and about 75% of Argentina''s vineyards lie in Mendoza — making it the single most important place on the planet for the grape and the global epicenter of Malbec.","source":"winefolly.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Mendoza?","a":"Late February through April — harvest and the Fiesta Nacional de la Vendimia (2026 central acts Mar 6–10) — is the most atmospheric window. Spring (Oct–Nov) is the value-and-balance alternative, with rates running ~15–25% below harvest peaks; either way, book icon wineries and lodges 3–4 months ahead of the Feb–April peak.","source":"across-southamerica.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"Which honeymoon wine-lodge should we book?","a":"The two ultra beds are Awasi Mendoza (Relais & Châteaux, Luján de Cuyo, 18 adobe rooms/villas on a ~60-acre private vineyard) and The Vines Resort & Spa (Valle de Uco, 21 private villas across 1,500 acres with vine-side dining). Both commission best through luxury consortia (Virtuoso/Fora), typically ~10%+ plus amenities.","source":"scottdunn.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you see Aconcagua on a day trip from Mendoza?","a":"Yes. Route 7 climbs the Alta Montaña corridor past Potrerillos (1,350 m), Uspallata (1,900 m), and Puente del Inca (2,720 m) to the Aconcagua Provincial Park viewpoint of the 6,961 m peak, the highest in the Western Hemisphere. The day-trip tops out ~2,700 m (mild breathlessness possible); Aconcagua summit mountaineering is a separate, expedition-grade activity requiring permits and licensed guides.","source":"getyourguide.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Mendoza safe?","a":"Yes. Argentina is a stable U.S. State Department Level 1 \"Exercise Normal Precautions\" country (updated 2026-05-20), and Mendoza is a mainstream wine-tourism destination. The only elevated carve-out is a Level 2 for the city of Rosario, ~1,000 km away in Santa Fe province — a different region entirely.","source":"travel.state.gov, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Mendoza?","a":"Drink-driving. Wine touring plus self-drive is the single most important avoidable risk, so the standard doctrine is always a designated driver or a guided wine tour with transport — never self-drive between tastings, and ride sober on the Maipú bike-and-wine route.","source":"machupicchu.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is Mendoza River rafting dangerous?","a":"Guided, it is a managed risk. Rafting at Potrerillos runs Class II–III, up to Class IV in high summer flow, with certified rescue guides, kayak safety support, and full neoprene/helmet/PFD standard — book certified operators only, and never run the river unguided.","source":"solsalute.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mendoza & Argentina Wine Country — Malbec, Valle de Uco & the Andes | TravelWell","search_language":"es-AR","local_keywords":["bodegas Mendoza","Valle de Uco vinos","Ruta del Vino Mendoza","Vendimia","Alta Montaña Aconcagua","termas de Cacheuta","Malbec de altura"],"hreflang":["en","es-AR"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Awasi Mendoza (formerly Cavas Wine Lodge)","brand":"Relais & Châteaux","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"18 adobe rooms/villas on ~60-acre private vineyard","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"The Vines Resort & Spa","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"21 private vineyard villas on 1,500 acres + spa + vine-side dining","earning":"consortia commission + villa MoR","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Casa de Uco","area":"Valle de Uco","product":"modern estate rooms, pool + spa, working-vineyard finca","earning":"consortia / DMC commission","tier":"premier"},{"name":"Entre Cielos","area":"Luján de Cuyo","product":"design hotel in 3.2 ha Malbec vines + Hammam spa circuit","earning":"consortia / bedbank premium","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Mendoza & the Wine Country, Argentina, Argentina"},"geo":{"lat":-32.8895,"lng":-68.8458}}'::jsonb, 67),
  ('merida-mexico', '10S', 'Mérida, Yucatán', 'Mexico', 'Mérida Yucatán travel guide', 'live', 'verified', 'kyoto', 'Yucatán (Mérida & Chichén Itzá)', '{"romance","expedition","culture","culinary"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, null, '{"key_facts":["Capital of Yucatán state and the peninsula''s cultural + medical hub; nicknamed ''La Ciudad Blanca'' (the White City).","Yucatán is US State Department Level 1 (Exercise Normal Precautions) — one of only two Level-1 Mexican states; the safest tier.","Heart of the restored-hacienda hotel circuit — Chablé, four Luxury Collection haciendas, Angsana Xcanatún — the region''s signature luxury supply.","Distinct Yucatecan cuisine (cochinita pibil, sopa de lima, mucbipollo) centered on the 1887 Mercado Lucas de Gálvez (~2,000 stalls).","Gateway to cenote country, Celestún/Río Lagartos flamingos, Uxmal + Ruta Puuc, and Chichén Itzá; Gulf beach at Progreso ~35 min north."],"safety":{"emergency":"911","hospital":"Star Médica Mérida; Christus Muguerza Faro del Mayab; Centro Médico de las Américas (CMA); Clínica de Mérida — regional trauma/medical hub","advisory_level":"L1","book_enabled":true,"air_access_verified":"MID — Mérida Manuel Crescencio Rejón International (direct US: DFW, IAH, MIA)","heat":"Hot-humid May–Sep; Apr–Jun can exceed 100°F (38°C) — extreme-heat protocol on daytime ruin/cenote outings","water":"Bottled only (do not drink tap; use bottled for tooth-brushing)","malaria":"No malaria risk in Mérida / Yucatán tourist corridor; dengue present, chikungunya rising (2025–26) — mosquito precautions"},"timing":{"inflection_curve_start":"~2026-10-25 (Hanal Pixán opening; late-Oct heat break + end of hurricane season lifts demand off baseline)","peak":"December–April (tightest Dec–March; dry-cool, low humidity)","fire_date":"2026-10-10","shoulder":"November; late April–early May","green":"May–September (hot-humid; Apr–Jun can exceed 100°F/38°C; rains peak Jun–Sep)","booking_lead":"Hacienda weddings 6–12 months (advised 10–12); leisure 1–3 months, longer for Hanal Pixán week","off_season_specials":"Summer hacienda + mansion-boutique rate softening; cenote-and-spa ''White City in the Green Season'' packaging; indoor culture year-round","event_peaks":["Hanal Pixán / Festival de las Ánimas (Oct 25–Nov 2)","Mérida Fest (early-mid January; 2026 ran Jan 5–18)","Flamingo season Nov–Feb (Celestún / Río Lagartos)"]},"jewels":[{"name":"Paseo de Montejo mansions (Casa Museo Montes Molina)","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The gilded-age face of Yucatán''s ''green gold''","bookable_category":"guided walking tour","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"Viator/local guide affiliate","source":"https://www.kupi.com/en-ae/explore/mexico/merida/paseo-de-montejo","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The gilded-age face of Yucatán''s ''green gold''","when":"December–April","commission":"Viator/local guide affiliate"},{"name":"Gran Museo del Mundo Maya","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The intellectual on-ramp before your first ruin","bookable_category":"entry + guided combo","tier":"essential","commission_path":"affiliate (entry non-commissionable)","source":"https://travel.usnews.com/Merida_Mexico/Things_To_Do/El_Gran_Museo_del_Mundo_Maya_de_Mrida_65503/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The intellectual on-ramp before your first ruin","when":"December–April","commission":"affiliate (entry non-commissionable)"},{"name":"Izamal — The Yellow Town + Convento de San Antonio","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The most photogenic town in Yucatán","bookable_category":"private day-trip + transfer","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC/Viator commissionable","source":"https://traveltomerida.com/best-day-trips-from-merida/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The most photogenic town in Yucatán","when":"December–April","commission":"DMC/Viator commissionable"},{"name":"Uxmal + Ruta Puuc","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The connoisseur''s Chichén — grander, emptier","bookable_category":"guided ruin circuit","tier":"premier","commission_path":"DMC/Viator commissionable","source":"https://www.viator.com/tours/Merida/UXMAL-ROUTE-HACIENDAS-AND-CENOTES/d5195-148085P1","si":"culture","blurb":"The connoisseur''s Chichén — grander, emptier","commission":"DMC/Viator commissionable"},{"name":"Chichén Itzá day-trip","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"The bucket-list ruin, done heat-smart at dawn","bookable_category":"guided day-tour + transfer","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC/Viator affiliate","source":"https://traveltomerida.com/best-day-trips-from-merida/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culture","blurb":"The bucket-list ruin, done heat-smart at dawn","when":"December–April","commission":"DMC/Viator affiliate"},{"name":"Mercado Lucas de Gálvez + cochinita pibil","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"All of Yucatán in one riot of color and smell","bookable_category":"food walking tour","tier":"essential","commission_path":"Viator/local affiliate + guide","source":"https://travelyucatan.com/merida-itinerary/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"culinary","blurb":"All of Yucatán in one riot of color and smell","when":"December–April","commission":"Viator/local affiliate + guide"},{"name":"Ixi''im at Chablé Yucatán (1,000-bottle tequila cellar)","si_tag":"Culinary","status":"future","hook":"Dinner as a cellar tour","bookable_category":"dining within a stay","tier":"ultra","commission_path":"Fora/Virtuoso (stay)","source":"https://yucatan.chablehotels.com/cuisine/ixiim/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culinary","blurb":"Dinner as a cellar tour","when":"year-round","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso (stay)"},{"name":"Hacienda-wedding circuit (Temozón/Santa Rosa/San José/Xcanatún/Sac Chich)","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"Married inside living history — chapel ruins + cenote gardens","bookable_category":"venue buyout + room block + planner","tier":"ultra","commission_path":"Fora/Virtuoso room block + wedding DMC","source":"https://www.destinationweddings.com/hacienda-san-jose-a-luxury-collection-hotel-san-jose","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"Married inside living history — chapel ruins + cenote gardens","when":"December–April","commission":"Fora/Virtuoso room block + wedding DMC"},{"name":"Rosas & Xocolate honeymoon suite","si_tag":"Romance & Honeymoons","status":"live","hook":"City-romance base with a rooftop and a story","bookable_category":"boutique hotel stay","tier":"premier","commission_path":"Marriott Bonvoy/STARS — Fora/Virtuoso","source":"https://yucatantoday.com/en/blog/rosas-y-xocolate-a-luxury-food-and-lodging-icon-in-merida","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","blurb":"City-romance base with a rooftop and a story","when":"December–April","commission":"Marriott Bonvoy/STARS — Fora/Virtuoso"},{"name":"Celestún flamingo biosphere boat safari","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Pink clouds at the edge of the Gulf","bookable_category":"guided day-trip + boat","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC/Viator (boat fee pass-through)","source":"https://www.girlwiththepassport.com/best-day-trips-from-merida-mexico/","si":"expedition","blurb":"Pink clouds at the edge of the Gulf","commission":"DMC/Viator (boat fee pass-through)"},{"name":"Río Lagartos + Las Coloradas","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Flamingos and rose-pink water in one frame","bookable_category":"long day-trip / overnight","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC commissionable","source":"https://www.girlwiththepassport.com/best-day-trips-from-merida-mexico/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Flamingos and rose-pink water in one frame","when":"December–April","commission":"DMC commissionable"},{"name":"Cuzamá / Homún cenote country (rail-cart)","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"The most Indiana-Jones way to reach turquoise water","bookable_category":"guided cenote-country day-trip","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"DMC/Viator (cenote entry pass-through)","source":"https://traveltomerida.com/best-day-trips-from-merida/","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"The most Indiana-Jones way to reach turquoise water","when":"December–April","commission":"DMC/Viator (cenote entry pass-through)"},{"name":"Cenotes de Mucuyché / Santa Bárbara","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"Both cenote personalities in one day — open + cavern","bookable_category":"private cenote tour","tier":"comfort","commission_path":"Viator/DMC","source":"https://www.tripadvisor.com/AttractionProductReview-g150811-d21491998-Private_Tour_Cenotes_of_Mucuyche_Santa_Barbara_in_one_day-Merida_Yucatan_Peninsula.html","timing":"December–April","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"expedition","blurb":"Both cenote personalities in one day — open + cavern","when":"December–April","commission":"Viator/DMC"},{"name":"Progreso Gulf beach + Malecón + world''s-longest pier","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","hook":"The city''s ocean, 30 minutes away","bookable_category":"transfer + beach-club day","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC/affiliate","source":"https://yucatan.guide/posts/progreso-beach-complete-visiting-guide","si":"expedition","blurb":"The city''s ocean, 30 minutes away","commission":"DMC/affiliate"},{"name":"Dzibilchaltún ruins + Cenote Xlacah","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","hook":"Ruin + swim + museum in a half-day","bookable_category":"guided half-day","tier":"essential","commission_path":"DMC/Viator (INAH fee pass-through)","source":"https://traveltomerida.com/best-day-trips-from-merida/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","si":"culture","blurb":"Ruin + swim + museum in a half-day","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC/Viator (INAH fee pass-through)"}],"faq":[{"q":"Is Mérida safe right now?","a":"Yes — it is the safest tier in Mexico. Yucatán carries US State Dept Level 1 \"Exercise Normal Precautions,\" the lowest rating, and with Campeche is one of only two Mexican states at Level 1 — a risk band comparable to Costa Rica or Belize. Mérida is also the regional trauma and medical hub, with four major private hospitals, an underrated safety asset for older travelers.","source":"travel.state.gov, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Why is Mérida the hacienda-wedding capital, and how far ahead do I book?","a":"Because the restored henequen haciendas — chapel ruins, walled gardens, private cenotes — are a wedding backdrop found nowhere else, backed by a mature, English-fluent planner ecosystem. Book the date and core vendors 6–12 months out (advisors say 10–12 for high season), the longest-lead, highest-margin flow in the destination.","source":"destinationweddings.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What are the best day-trips from Mérida?","a":"Cenotes and flamingos, mostly within ~1.5 hr. The closest swimmable cenote and ruin is Dzibilchaltún (~20 min); the Cuzamá/Homún cenote country is reached by horse-drawn rail-cart (~1 hr); Celestún''s flamingo biosphere is ~1.5 hr west; and Uxmal + the Ruta Puuc lie ~1.5 hr south. Chichén Itzá is ~1.5 hr east, best done at dawn.","source":"girlwiththepassport.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Mérida?","a":"December through April is the dry-cool peak (highs ~84°F, lows ~64°F), but the smartest window is the late-October Hanal Pixán opening (Oct 25–Nov 2), when the heat breaks and hurricane season ends — the Festival de las Ánimas fills the streets with altars and the candlelit Paseo de las Ánimas, mostly free to attend. November and late April are softer-rate shoulders.","source":"plalla.com / traveltomerida.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What should I eat in Mérida?","a":"Yucatecan food, which stands apart from central-Mexican cooking. The signature is cochinita pibil — pork marinated in achiote and bitter orange, wrapped in banana leaves and slow-roasted in an underground pit — best at the 1887 Mercado Lucas de Gálvez (~2,000 stalls), alongside sopa de lima, papadzules, salbutes and panuchos.","source":"travelyucatan.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Mérida?","a":"Heat, not crime. May–September is hot-humid and April–June can exceed 100°F (38°C), so run daytime ruin and cenote-country outings on an extreme-heat protocol: dawn starts, hat and high SPF, electrolytes, a midday shade break, and no midday Chichén or Uxmal in summer. Drink bottled water only, and use repellent — dengue is present and chikungunya rose in 2025–26 (no malaria in the corridor).","source":"traveltomerida.com, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is cenote diving near Mérida safe?","a":"Yes when the guided/unguided line is respected. Cenote swimming and snorkeling need only swimming ability; a \"cenote dive\" should be a guided cavern dive that stays in the daylight zone with a certified cave-guide leading. True cave penetration is technical, Full-Cave-only, and not a tourist activity. Carry DAN/DiveAssure dive-accident insurance, observe no-fly for 18–24 h, and know the nearest recompression chambers are on Cozumel, not Mérida.","source":"prodiveinternational.com / costamed.com.mx, 2026-07-06","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Mérida, Yucatán Travel Guide 2026 — Haciendas, Cenotes & the White City | TravelWell.World","meta_description":"Plan Mérida, Yucatán — Mexico''s safest state (US Level 1). Luxury hacienda hotels, cenote day-trips, Chichén Itzá & Uxmal, Progreso beach, Hanal Pixán, and hacienda weddings.","slug":"merida-mexico","primary_keyword":"Mérida Yucatán travel guide","long_tail":["best time to visit Mérida Mexico","Yucatán hacienda hotels","cenotes near Mérida","Mérida hacienda wedding","Chichén Itzá day trip from Mérida","Hanal Pixán Mérida","is Mérida Mexico safe"],"search_language":"en + es-MX","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Mérida","haciendas Yucatán boda","cenotes cerca de Mérida","mejor época para visitar Mérida","Hanal Pixán Mérida","haciendas de lujo Yucatán"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","author_byline":"By David McCallister — commercial pilot, 56 countries","content_freshness":"2026-07-06"},"booking":null,"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"Romance & Honeymoons (RHN)","status":"live"},{"si":"Global Expedition Adventures (GEA)","status":"live"},{"si":"culture","status":"future"},{"si":"culinary","status":"future"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Chablé Yucatán","why_ultra":"Leading Hotels of the World; 38 private-pool forest villas; sacred-cenote spa; 1,000+ bottle tequila cellar; Ixi''im destination restaurant","earning":"LHW Leaders Club / Virtuoso preferred booking — commission + amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"Upgrade on arrival, daily breakfast, spa/resort credit, early check-in / late check-out","mor":"Hotel (LHW) bills guest; TWW = advisor-of-record","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Hacienda Temozón, a Luxury Collection Hotel","why_ultra":"17th-c. henequen hacienda; 28 rooms incl. owner''s-bedroom Presidential Suite; cenote spa","earning":"Marriott Luxury Collection / STARS — commission + STARS amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS: $100 property credit, room upgrade, breakfast, early/late, welcome amenity","mor":"Marriott bills guest; TWW = STARS advisor","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Hacienda San José Cholul, a Luxury Collection Hotel","why_ultra":"15-suite henequen hacienda; open-air 19th-c. architecture; weddings to 300 guests","earning":"Marriott Luxury Collection / STARS — commission + amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS amenity suite (credit, upgrade, breakfast, early/late)","mor":"Marriott bills guest; TWW = STARS advisor","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Hacienda Xcanatún, Angsana Heritage Collection","why_ultra":"18th-c. sisal hacienda, 54 suites, ~25 min from Centro; Virtuoso-listed; strong weddings/honeymoons","earning":"Accor/Angsana; Virtuoso preferred — commission + amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"Virtuoso amenity: property credit, upgrade, breakfast, early/late","mor":"Accor bills guest; TWW = Virtuoso advisor","tier":"luxury"},{"name":"Rosas & Xocolate","why_ultra":"17-room Design Hotel boutique from two 1930s Paseo de Montejo mansions; the in-city ultra-boutique romance base","earning":"Marriott Bonvoy / Design Hotels / STARS-eligible — commission + amenities","virtuoso_value_add":"STARS/Bonvoy amenity + upgrade","mor":"Marriott bills guest; TWW = advisor","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":"2026-07-06","hero":{"query":"Mérida, Yucatán, Mexico"},"geo":{"lat":20.9674,"lng":-89.5926}}'::jsonb, 68)
